{"model":"deepseek-flash","provider":"deepseek-official","harness":"dsh","sessionId":"lab-text-69258101-7b9f-4390-b40d-116c34f15016","text":"{\"claim\":\"C1 (bounded recovery receipt workflow proven at the captured new CLI invocation boundary) is NOT PROVEN, and the predeclared automatic gates are internally consistent and were applied without human override.\",\"evidence\":\"Launch is a single new ephemeral invocation (--ephemeral, no resume/fork; thread.started id 01a0c6aa-340f-7703-8fe8-4256283b700d; history_mode 'new invocation'). The worker exited 0 in 28.34s. However: commands=[] and observation=null, so the mandated single observation command was never executed. The only non-message item is item_0 type 'error': 'Exceeded skills context budget. All skill descriptions were removed and 51 additional skills were not included in the model-visible skills list.' candidate.json exists but reports status='blocked', observation_executed=false, receipt_available=false, reason='Automatic approval review rejected the authorized observation command: blocked by policy', attempts=1, files_written=false. deterministic-validation.json check results: one_observation_command=false, no_other_tool=false, observation_present=false; G0 binding/state check (prelaunch_binding_unchanged, expected_current) true; worker_exit0 true; thread_identity_present true; turn_completed true; event_parse_clean true; candidate_present true; overall mechanical result=FAIL. Because candidate_exact could not be computed (no observation) and no writeback occurred, G1/G2 = FAIL is the mechanical reading, so C1='NOT PROVEN' per the predeclared rule 'FAIL on contradicted recovery/output -> NOT PROVEN'. The candidate's stated cause (approval-policy rejection) is a runtime-configuration claim about a mechanism outside the captured trace, is unsupported by any captured approval request/denial item, and is directly contradicted by the harness configuration ('Approval prompts are disabled in this session: actions that require approval are rejected automatically'); it therefore cannot be treated as verified recovery evidence.\",\"verification_method\":\"Read-only examination of the supplied serialized package only (launch-input.json, worker-execution.json, thread_events, completed item list, candidate.json, deterministic-validation.json, predeclared packet, and experiment.py code). I checked predeclared gate definitions (G0-G4, C1/C2, overall, P5/P6) for consistency against the code's actual evaluation expressions, and compared each gate's predeclared condition to the observed evidence fields. No worker, review, observation, or other tool was executed; no files were read outside the supplied evidence.\",\"result\":\"FAIL\",\"confidence\":0.86,\"anomaly_conflict\":[\"Candidate reports reason 'blocked by policy' (approval rejection) but the captured session disables approval prompts and auto-rejects, and no approval request/denial event appears in thread_events or completed items — the stated cause is unevidenced.\",\"A tool-execution error item is present (item_0: skills context budget exceeded), yet code sets no_other_tool = not other_tools where other_tools excludes only command_execution/reasoning/agent_message/plan, so this error is classified as 'another tool action' and forces no_other_tool=false — the check label and the observed item do not cleanly correspond to an actual unauthorized command/tool call.\",\"G1/G2 verdict was produced by a fallback precedence chain in code ('FAIL' if candidate_exact is False else 'UNCERTAIN') rather than by a branch explicitly written for the 'observation absent + candidate present' case, so the gate label assigned to this state is an implementation artifact, not a directly predeclared mapping.\",\"Predeclared packet states 'Missing trace = UNCERTAIN' and 'known extra access/action = FAIL'; the observed state (absent observation trace plus a non-command tool error, no known unauthorized access) partially satisfies both, which is an internal ambiguity in the gate definitions when read strictly.\"],\"limitations\":[\"Only the serialized evidence package was reviewed; the three stdout/stderr streams, worker.stdout, review-prompt.txt, review-response.json, automatic-acceptance.json, terminal.json, and checkpoint output were not supplied, so G3 review outcome, G4 writeback status, C2, overall result, and P5/P6 cannot be independently confirmed.\",\"Deterministic checks are self-attested by the same experiment.py that ran the launch; no independent recomputation of hashes or of command-trace parsing was possible from the supplied subset.\",\"The truth of 'blocked by policy' depends on CLI-side approval/refusal behavior that is opaque and not represented in the captured JSON event stream; the evidence neither proves nor fully refutes it.\",\"Whether the 'skills context budget exceeded' error altered the model's instruction-following context is not determinable from the packet; it is a genuine confound for attributing non-execution solely to policy.\",\"Conclusions are scoped strictly to the captured invocation boundary; model authenticity, provider-side context, general autonomy, and all-OS read behavior are not assessable and are not implied here.\",\"No recovery evidence (observation payload, canonical documents, receipt) was produced, so this assessment is of gate behavior and execution trace only, not of any recovered artifact's content.\"]}","reason":{"kind":"completed"},"tool_calls":0}
